            {
              "id": "4",
              "guid": "82f78639-b139-4a31-868e-17fb34ce5fa6",
              "deleted": true,
              "heading": "User Roles",
              "instructions": "<p>Identify user roles for the product and for each role describe characteristics of a typical user.</p><p>You may consider creating personas with a real name. Each persona should be described sufficiently that everyone on the team feels like they know the persona.</p>",
              "type": "SEC",
              "history": [
                {
                  "attributesChanged": {
                    "deleted": null
                  },
                  "changedBy": {
                    "company": "UNIVERSIDAD PONTIFICIA BOLIVARIANA",
                    "email": "federmarquezcalle@gmail.com",
                    "name": "FEDERICO MARQUEZ"
                  },
                  "changedOn": "2026-07-28T05:40:29.252Z"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "5",
          "guid": "d7375477-1699-445b-9a4b-2ca87dfce40f",
          "deleted": true,
          "heading": "User Stories",
          "instructions": "<p>Specify user stories describing functionality of the product grouped into <em>epics</em> for easier navigation in the document.</p><p>Set the following attributes for each story:</p><ul><li><em>Heading:</em> short story name,</li><li><em>As a(n):</em> type of user,</li><li><em>I want:</em> some goal,</li><li><em>So that:&nbsp;</em>some reason,</li><li><em>Acceptance Criteria:</em> more details how the story should be verified and providing the basic criteria that can be used to determine if a story is fully implemented,</li><li><em>Priority:</em> “High” for fundamental features, “Medium” for important features having a short-term workaround, “Low” for features which can be left out of the release if time runs out or won't-have for features will be needed in a later release,</li><li><em>Risk:</em> “High”, “Medium”, or “Low”,</li><li><em>Estimation:</em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>story points which are relative estimate of the complexity, effort or duration of a story, and</li><li><em>Status:&nbsp;</em> workflow information classifying stories as “New”, “Planned”, “Implemented” or “Verified”.</li></ul>",
          "type": "SEC",
          "history": [
            {
              "attributesChanged": {
                "deleted": null
              },
              "changedBy": {
                "company": "UNIVERSIDAD PONTIFICIA BOLIVARIANA",
                "email": "federmarquezcalle@gmail.com",
                "name": "FEDERICO MARQUEZ"
              },
              "changedOn": "2026-07-28T05:40:40.525Z"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "6",
          "guid": "f3b7db6d-3367-4bf7-a443-c2860732959b",
          "deleted": true,
          "heading": "Constraints",
          "instructions": "<p>Identify constraints addressing non-functional requirements about product performance, accuracy, portability, reusability, maintainability, interoperability, availability, usability, security and capacity.</p><p>Set the following constraint attributes:</p><ul><li><em>Heading:</em> short constraint name</li><li><em>Text:</em> constraint description</li><li><em>Acceptance Criteria:</em> more details how the constraint should be verified and providing the basic criteria that can be used to determine if the constraint is not violated</li></ul><p><br></p>",
          "type": "SEC",
          "history": [
            {
              "attributesChanged": {
                "deleted": null
              },
              "changedBy": {
                "company": "UNIVERSIDAD PONTIFICIA BOLIVARIANA",
                "email": "federmarquezcalle@gmail.com",
                "name": "FEDERICO MARQUEZ"
              },
              "changedOn": "2026-07-28T05:40:44.456Z"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
